                     "description":  "Print and cut one A4 sheet of 40mm seal stickers (\"Handmade Just For You\" badge on a white circle): **24 a sheet**, **one per order** (a split order gets one per parcel). SmithPackaging label sheet, Epson ET-3950, Cricut Print Then Cut. Regular paper is fine: the seal sits under Sellotape Zero Plastic.\r\n\r\n**First print only (then delete this list):**\r\n- [ ] In Design Space, with the lock on, check each seal is a **flattened 40mm white circle** with the badge centred (reads **4.0 × 4.0cm**). Note the project name and grid.\r\n- [ ] Confirm 4 across fits: they come to about 181mm against the ~183mm Print Then Cut width. If Design Space objects, fall back to **20 a sheet** (4 × 5, wider gaps).\r\n- [ ] Confirm the cut setting on a real label sheet: Sticker Paper, Kiss Cut, pressure Less (only tested on copy paper so far).\r\n- [ ] Confirm the sheet gives 24 good seals.\r\n- [ ] Decide whether stock counts in seals or sheets (output per run 24 or 1).\r\n\r\nFull reference: `claude/Internal-Products-Workflow.md` §2.",
